            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "Finally, the Excess Heat Factor (EHF) simultaneously reflects the combined effects of heat extremes and human adaptability in response to short-term temperature variability during heatwaves (Nairn et al. 2018; Nairn and Fawcett 2014). This index integrates the severity, frequency, and duration of heatwave events. Following Nairn and Fawcett (2013), a heatwave is defined as a period in which the EHF remains positive for three or more consecutive days.",
