            "target_entity_type": "Resolution",
            "paragraph": "To overcome these limitations, gridded datasets such as Spain02 (Herrera et al. 2012), Iberia01 (Herrera et al. 2019) d OBS (Cornes et al. 2018) have been increasingly used. Using Spain02, Lorenzo and Alvarez (2022) analyzed the SU and SU35 indices for the period 1971\u20132000. The results showed that the highest indices frequencies were located in the south of the peninsula over the Guadalquivir valley, with average annual values around 200 days for SU and 80 days for SU35. Fonseca et al. (2023), applying Iberia01, observed similar spatial patterns in Portuguese wine regions for the same period. Southern areas experienced high SU values, with more than 100 days per year, while northern regions had significantly lower values, generally below 50 days. Although these interpolated datasets improve coverage, their moderate resolution (approximately 0.1\u00b0) limits the capture of local variability in complex terrains.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "ERA5-Land",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SPATIAL_RESOLUTION",
            "target_entity_instance": "0.1\u00b0",
            "target_entity_type": "Resolution",
            "paragraph": "Another recent study by Yava\u015fl\u0131 and Erlat (2024) analyzed tropical nights across the Mediterranean using ERA5-Land (spatial resolution 0.1\u00b0) data from 1950 to 2022, and reported that the Iberian Mediterranean coast is among the most affected regions, with 40\u201380 tropical nights annually and up to 50 in the Guadalquivir and Ebro valleys.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
